# =============================================================================
# PRODUCTION env template — shared server + EXTERNAL Traefik (docs/07-deployment.md, ADR-017).
# Copy to `.env` ON THE SERVER into THAT instance's directory /opt/<dir> and fill from the secret
# manager. The instance -> /opt/<dir> roster is the LIVE INSTANCES list below (the SINGLE roster of
# this file; authoritative registry — docs/07-deployment.md §CI/CD-контракт: INSTANCES-loop).
# NEVER commit the real `.env` (it is gitignored). This `.example` holds PLACEHOLDERS ONLY —
# no real secrets.
#
# All secrets must come from the server's secret manager / env, never baked into the image
# (docs/05-security.md). Generate high-entropy secrets with:  openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Loaded by docker-compose.prod.yml via `env_file: .env` (api + migrate). The image is built
# ON THE SERVER from sources (no registry tag), so there is NO IMAGE/IMAGE_TAG here (ADR-017).
# =============================================================================

# --- Multi-instance identity (ADR-017 §Мульти-инстанс) -----------------------
# docker-compose project name = instance prefix. Substituted as ${COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME:-claude-ios}
# into the image tags (<proj>-backend:prod) and the Traefik router/service names (routers.<proj>).
# DEFAULT is `claude-ios` == the previous hardcoded value (backward-compat invariant: `compose
# config` is identical when this key is unset). PUBLIC config, not a secret.
# VALUE RULE (holds for present AND future instances, so adding one needs no edit of this rule):
#   - broadnova (/opt/claude-ios): LEAVE UNSET (commented out) -> resolves to `claude-ios` (no-op).
#   - any other instance (including any future clone): COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=<its own name>, which is
#     the basename of its /opt/<dir>. It is deployed with `-p <proj>` so its containers/volumes/
#     default-network are isolated. The shared `web` network and Traefik are common to all live
#     instances alike.
# LIVE INSTANCES — the SINGLE per-instance roster of this file. Every other section of this file
#   refers HERE instead of restating a list (a restated list rots the moment an instance is added,
#   which is exactly how the stale enumerations below it were born):
#   broadnova (/opt/claude-ios), avelyra (/opt/avelyra), orvianix (/opt/orvianix),
#   elvarixa (/opt/elvarixa), corvionet (/opt/corvionet), modavira (/opt/modavira),
#   artolixo (/opt/artolixo), lunexoro (/opt/lunexoro), ravionet (/opt/ravionet),
#   vireluma (/opt/vireluma), taluneri (/opt/taluneri), webmoria (/opt/webmoria),
#   velunixa (/opt/velunixa), ravelumi (/opt/ravelumi), qorimelo (/opt/qorimelo), zenquelo (/opt/zenquelo).
#   Authoritative registry (dir / project / SERVICE_DOMAIN / LLM provider per instance):
#   docs/07-deployment.md §CI/CD-контракт: INSTANCES-loop — нормативное значение = фактическое
#   `INSTANCES` в обоих workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml + deploy.yml). This roster MUST equal
#   that `INSTANCES`; on divergence the workflow value wins and this roster is corrected to match.
#   Every entry of this roster MUST also have its own row (dir / project / SERVICE_DOMAIN /
#   провайдер) in that registry table — a roster entry without a registry row is a docs defect,
#   because the sections below resolve domain and provider THROUGH that table.
# DECOMMISSIONED: veltrio (veltriohub.shop) was removed 2026-07-18 — containers deleted, Traefik
#   router dropped, the domain now belongs to a DIFFERENT service on the same server. Do NOT
#   provision /opt/veltrio and do NOT re-add it to INSTANCES: a re-created router would hijack a
#   domain that is no longer ours.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=avelyra

# --- Traefik routing (ADR-017) ----------------------------------------------
# Service domain — DUAL role:
#   1) Traefik Host router label Host(`${SERVICE_DOMAIN}`) and the ACME cert (ADR-017).
#   2) Read by the APP (ADR-031) to build the ABSOLUTE site.preview URL
#      https://<SERVICE_DOMAIN>/v1/preview/... so the model copies it verbatim (no host
#      hallucination). Same value, same var — no extra env needed; deploying the new code
#      picks it up because SERVICE_DOMAIN is part of the provisioned .env for the instances of the
#      LIVE INSTANCES roster above. Normalized app-side.
# PER-INSTANCE value — the instance -> domain mapping lives ONLY in the authoritative registry
# docs/07-deployment.md §CI/CD-контракт: INSTANCES-loop (table columns dir / project /
# SERVICE_DOMAIN) and is deliberately NOT duplicated here. The value below is broadnova's
# (/opt/claude-ios); an instance other than broadnova MUST overwrite it in its own
# /opt/<instance>/.env with that instance's own domain from that table.
# Q-017-1 (resolved): broadnova's domain is broadnova.shop. Its A-record MUST point to 87.239.135.154
# BEFORE launch (Traefik's Let's Encrypt ACME challenge). TLS/ACME is issued by the external
# Traefik, not by us. NOTE: this is PUBLIC config, not a secret.
SERVICE_DOMAIN=broadnova.shop
# ACME cert-resolver name configured in the SHARED Traefik (/opt/edge) by the server owner.
# Q-017-2 (resolved): the resolver name is `le` (default on the websecure entrypoint).
# PUBLIC config, not a secret.
TRAEFIK_CERTRESOLVER=le

# --- Database / Redis --------------------------------------------------------
# In-compose service names (internal `default` network). Credentials below MUST match
# POSTGRES_* (provisioned secrets).
# CLONE NOTE (ADR-017 §Мульти-инстанс): a clone's DATABASE_URL MUST reference its OWN
# POSTGRES_USER / POSTGRES_DB / POSTGRES_PASSWORD (a fresh `openssl rand -base64 32` password —
# never reuse a sibling instance's DB or credentials; volumes are isolated per project name).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://<db_user>:<db_password>@postgres:5432/<db_name>
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
# Postgres container bootstrap creds — REAL secrets in prod (secret manager).
POSTGRES_USER=<db_user>
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<db_password>
POSTGRES_DB=<db_name>

# --- LLM provider selection (ADR-033) ----------------------------------------
# Which LLM provider the orchestration uses: `anthropic` | `openai`. PER-INSTANCE, PUBLIC (not a
# secret). WHICH instance runs WHICH provider is recorded ONLY in the authoritative registry
# docs/07-deployment.md §CI/CD-контракт: INSTANCES-loop (column «провайдер») — not duplicated here,
# so a new instance changes the registry alone. DEFAULT `anthropic` == unchanged behaviour: an
# instance whose registry provider is Anthropic LEAVES THIS UNSET (commented) -> resolves to
# `anthropic` (no-op, compose/behaviour unchanged); an instance whose registry provider is OpenAI
# sets `LLM_PROVIDER=openai`.
#   - LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic -> default credits provider is Anthropic.
#   - LLM_PROVIDER=openai    -> default credits provider is OpenAI.
# Extra credits providers are OPT-IN via LLM_PROVIDERS (ADR-073); two keys alone do not enable dual.
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
#
# Dual-credits (ADR-073, OPT-IN). Unset/empty = only LLM_PROVIDER (live instances unchanged).
# Example to serve both catalogs on an OpenAI instance: LLM_PROVIDERS=openai,anthropic
# plus BOTH API keys and both * _MODELS allowlists. Two keys alone do NOT enable dual.
# LLM_PROVIDERS=

# --- Anthropic (mode=credits). Used when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic (default) or as extra credits
# via LLM_PROVIDERS (ADR-073). On a single-provider OpenAI instance this block is unused in
# credits-runtime; BYOK Anthropic keys still work via ADR-044.
# Real key WITH positive balance (prod-checklist, ready). SECRET — secret manager only.
# SHARING POLICY — one of the TWO documented exceptions to "a fresh secret per instance": this key
#   is taken AS IS from a sibling anthropic instance (the owner's single funded account) and is NOT
#   generated fresh for a clone. Authoritative: docs/07-deployment.md §Clone `.env`-контракт, row
#   `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` — a deliberate owner trade-off, not a defect to "fix": quotas, rate-limit
#   and billing are fleet-wide, and a leak is an incident of EVERY anthropic instance at once.
#   Nothing else is relaxed — every other secret of that contract stays per-instance and fresh.
#   NEVER commit a real value (placeholder below).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<anthropic_api_key>
# Spare Anthropic key (ADR-074). Optional. Alias: ANTHROPIC_FALLBACK_API_KEY.
# Empty = no Anthropic key rotation. SECRET — same sharing policy as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_BACKUP=<anthropic_api_key_backup>
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
# Output token budget per call (ADR-025). 16000 prevents truncation of code/file generation
# (stop_reason=max_tokens). Per-instance — set wherever this ANTHROPIC block applies (registry
# provider = Anthropic). On an instance with LLM_PROVIDER=openai use OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS instead.
# Non-streaming.
ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS=16000
# Raised to 120 (ADR-025) for long non-streaming generation at 16000 tokens.
ANTHROPIC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
ANTHROPIC_MAX_RETRIES=2

# --- OpenAI (mode=credits). Used when LLM_PROVIDER=openai (ADR-033) or as extra via LLM_PROVIDERS.
# Set this whole block on ANY instance whose registry provider is OpenAI (LLM_PROVIDER=openai);
# which instances those are is read from the authoritative registry docs/07-deployment.md
# §CI/CD-контракт: INSTANCES-loop (column «провайдер»). On an instance whose registry provider is
# Anthropic leave this block unset/commented (ANTHROPIC_* is used instead).
# OPENAI_API_KEY — SECRET, secret manager only, under redaction. REQUIRED when LLM_PROVIDER=openai.
#   SHARING POLICY — one of the TWO documented exceptions to "a fresh secret per instance": this key
#   is taken AS IS from a sibling OpenAI instance (the owner's single funded account) and is NOT
#   generated fresh for a clone. Authoritative: docs/07-deployment.md §Clone `.env`-контракт, row
#   `OPENAI_API_KEY` — a deliberate owner trade-off (2026-08-07), not a defect to "fix": quotas,
#   rate-limit and billing are fleet-wide, and a leak is an incident of EVERY OpenAI instance at
#   once. Nothing else is relaxed — every other secret of that contract stays per-instance and
#   fresh. NEVER commit a real value (placeholder below). On an Anthropic instance this is not set.
OPENAI_API_KEY=<openai_api_key>
# Spare OpenAI key (ADR-074). Optional. Alias: OPEN_AI_BACK_UP_API_KEY.
# Empty = no OpenAI key rotation. SECRET — same sharing policy as OPENAI_API_KEY.
# OPENAI_API_KEY_BACKUP=<openai_api_key_backup>
# Anthropic model used when BOTH OpenAI keys are banned/out of funds (ADR-074).
# Empty = no OpenAI→Anthropic hop. Does not change GET /v1/models or LLM_PROVIDER.
# OPENAI_CHAT_FALLBACK_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
# OpenAI model used when Anthropic upstream fails (ADR-074). Empty = no Anthropic→OpenAI hop.
# ANTHROPIC_CHAT_FALLBACK_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o
# Default orchestration model (Responses API in production, Chat Completions fallback). Default gpt-4o.
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o
# Output token budget per call. Default 16000 (parity with ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS).
OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS=16000
# Upstream call timeout, seconds. Default 120.
OPENAI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# SDK retries. Default 2.
OPENAI_MAX_RETRIES=2
# Active model returned in the BYOK response (activeModel) when keyStatus=valid (ADR-016/ADR-033).
# Separate from anthropic BYOK_DEFAULT_MODEL. Default gpt-4o.
OPENAI_BYOK_DEFAULT_MODEL=gpt-4o

# --- JWT (RS256) — embedded issuer (ADR-018) ---------------------------------
# The backend signs and verifies its own RS256 tokens. Generate an RSA keypair on the
# server (openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 -out jwt_private.pem;
# openssl rsa -in jwt_private.pem -pubout -out jwt_public.pem), mount via .secrets/ and point
# the *_PATH vars at them. Without a private key /v1/auth/* returns 503 (verify still works).
# JWT_ISSUER is PER-INSTANCE = https://<that instance's SERVICE_DOMAIN> — the same domain that
# instance sets in SERVICE_DOMAIN above (mapping instance -> domain: registry table
# docs/07-deployment.md §CI/CD-контракт: INSTANCES-loop; not duplicated here). Below is broadnova's.
# Each instance also has its OWN keypair (never shared between instances).
JWT_ISSUER=https://broadnova.shop
JWT_AUDIENCE=claude-ios
JWT_KID=mvp-key-1
# Keys by file path (recommended) — mounted read-only into the api container (.secrets/).
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/app/.secrets/jwt_private.pem
JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PATH=/app/.secrets/jwt_public.pem
# Alternative inline PEM (\n-escaped, single line); leave empty when using *_PATH.
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=
JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=
# External-IdP verify-only mode (Apple/Firebase) — leave empty for embedded issuer.
JWT_JWKS_URL=
# Token TTLs (embedded issuer).
AUTH_ACCESS_TTL_SECONDS=3600
AUTH_REFRESH_TTL_SECONDS=2592000
AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP=10

# --- KMS envelope encryption for BYOK (ADR-003, LocalKmsClient on MVP) -------
# High-entropy 32-byte master key, base64. SECRET — secret manager only, under redaction.
# KMS_KEY_ID is EMPTY on MVP (LocalKmsClient, in-process AES-256-GCM wrap; no cloud KMS yet —
# Q-002-1). A clone uses its OWN fresh KMS_LOCAL_MASTER_KEY (BYOK ciphertext is NOT portable
# between instances, by design — ADR-003 §Мульти-инстанс clone contract).
KMS_KEY_ID=
KMS_LOCAL_MASTER_KEY=<base64-32-random-bytes>

# --- App Store Server API (Q-007-1) ------------------------------------------
# must-configure-before-launch: production posture + Apple root CA + real bundle id.
APPSTORE_ENVIRONMENT=production
APPSTORE_BUNDLE_ID=<com.example.app>
# Apple root CA directory for REAL StoreKit JWS verification (subscription/storekit.py).
# The IN-CONTAINER path is PINNED by docker-compose.prod.yml (`environment: APPSTORE_ROOT_CERT_DIR=
# /etc/appstore-certs`), which bind-mounts the HOST dir `./certs/appstore` (-> /opt/<instance>/
# certs/appstore) read-only. So this `.env` value is INFORMATIONAL — compose overrides it; you do
# NOT need to set it here. To enable real verification, drop AppleRootCA-G3.cer (public,
# https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/) into /opt/<instance>/certs/appstore on the server
# and restart api (see the §Apple root CA provisioning runbook at the bottom of this file).
# EMPTY dir -> _load_roots()=[] -> StoreKit stays test-mode / fail-closed (container starts fine).
APPSTORE_ROOT_CERT_DIR=/etc/appstore-certs

# --- StoreKit test-mode — MUST be false in prod (Q-007-1, TD-007) ------------
# Prod fail-closed: real JWS verification. Leave TEST_SECRET empty in prod.
# DEV/TEST ONLY flag for local/sandbox runs without Apple root-chain anchoring. In production
# it must remain false; the verifier also ignores it when APPSTORE_ENVIRONMENT=production.
STOREKIT_DEV_SKIP_CERT_CHAIN_VERIFICATION=false
STOREKIT_TEST_MODE=false
STOREKIT_TEST_SECRET=

# --- Billing (ADR-006) -------------------------------------------------------
SUBSCRIPTION_CREDITS_PER_PERIOD=1000
# Generation-mode prices for the existing wallet. `general` is the legacy ordinary chat cost;
# `research` enables hosted web search; `reasoning` enables provider reasoning/thinking;
# `study_learn` returns a quiz pool instead of plain text.
# All four are clamped to >= 1: a 0/negative value cannot make a mode free.
CHAT_CREDIT_COST_GENERAL=1
CHAT_CREDIT_COST_RESEARCH=3
CHAT_CREDIT_COST_REASONING=3
CHAT_CREDIT_COST_STUDY_LEARN=2
# Modes this instance ADVERTISES in GET /v1/chat/v2/capabilities (comma-separated).
# Advertisement gate only: /v1/chat/v2/run accepts every mode on every instance regardless.
# Unset/blank/all-invalid => general,research,reasoning (fail-closed): `study_learn` is advertised
# ONLY where the app can render the quiz, otherwise the user picks it and gets an empty screen for
# 2 credits. `general` is always included. Unknown values are ignored with a WARNING.
CHAT_ADVERTISED_GENERATION_MODES=general,research,reasoning
CHAT_REASONING_LEVEL=medium
ANTHROPIC_THINKING_BUDGET_TOKENS=4096
ANTHROPIC_THINKING_DISPLAY=omitted
ANTHROPIC_WEB_SEARCH_TOOL_TYPE=web_search_20260318

# --- Token purchase (ADR-015) — NOT a secret, but must match App Store Connect IAP -----
# Server-side mapping consumable productId -> credits (JSON). Unknown productId -> 422.
TOKEN_PRODUCTS={"tokens_1500":1500,"tokens_600":600,"tokens_250":250,"tokens_100":100}

# --- Image/video generation via fal.ai (ADR-060) ------------------------------
# FAL_API_KEY — SECRET, PER-INSTANCE (own fal account balance; never share between instances).
#   Empty => the whole /v1/media/* surface answers 503 media_generation_not_configured, i.e. the
#   feature is opt-in per instance. Sent upstream as `Authorization: Key <...>` (fal's own scheme,
#   NOT Bearer); never logged, never returned, never persisted. NEVER commit a real value.
FAL_API_KEY=<set-per-instance to enable /v1/media/*; leave empty to keep generation off>
# PUBLIC upstream QUEUE host (async submit/poll). The synchronous fal.run host cannot serve
# minute-long Kling/Veo runs. Change only if fal moves the host. Also the allowlist for the
# polling URLs fal returns (SSRF guard), so it must match the host fal actually replies with.
FAL_QUEUE_BASE=https://queue.fal.run
# Connect+read timeout (s) of ONE fal HTTP call. Bounds submit/status/result only — the generation
# runs in fal's queue and is polled, so raising this does not extend the generation budget.
FAL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
# Per-model credit price override (JSON {modelId: credits}); NOT a secret. Models absent here keep
# the registry default for the 1K / one-pack cell (nano-banana-2=4, nano-banana-pro=8,
# kling-video=5, kling-video-v3=10, veo-3.1=15). Image resolution tiers and Veo 4k/audio
# multipliers stay relative to that base. A non-positive / non-int value is DROPPED, so a typo
# cannot make a run free; the
# price is never taken from the request body. Clients read it from GET /v1/media/models, so
# repricing needs no iOS release. Calibrate against the real fal invoice (Q-060-3).
MEDIA_MODEL_CREDITS={}
# Max jobs returned by one page of GET /v1/media/jobs.
MEDIA_JOBS_PAGE_LIMIT=50
# Empty = fal default (>=7 days, then the asset URL dies). 0 = never expire. N = N seconds.
FAL_ASSET_RETENTION_SECONDS=0
# Reference-image upload for image-to-image / image-to-video (ADR-062).
FAL_REST_BASE=https://rest.fal.ai
FAL_UPLOAD_HOST_SUFFIXES=.fal.ai,.fal.media,.fal.run,.storage.googleapis.com
MEDIA_UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES=10485760
# Must stay >= ceil(MEDIA_UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES * 4/3) + JSON overhead.
MEDIA_UPLOAD_REQUEST_BODY_LIMIT=16777216
# Gallery template covers (ADR-066): decoded cover ceiling + raised body limit for
# POST /v1/admin/media/templates only (not the 8 KB admin cap).
MEDIA_TEMPLATE_COVER_MAX_BYTES=2097152
MEDIA_TEMPLATE_COVER_REQUEST_BODY_LIMIT=4194304
# Background reconciler for non-terminal media jobs (ADR-067 / Q-060-2). <=0 disables.
MEDIA_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECONDS=15
MEDIA_RECONCILE_BATCH_SIZE=50

# --- APNs push (ADR-067 / TD-011) — PER-INSTANCE --------------------------------
# Empty credentials => device-token CRUD works; send is a no-op (warning). NEVER commit real .p8.
APNS_KEY_ID=<10-char Key ID from Apple Developer>
APNS_TEAM_ID=<10-char Team ID>
# PEM contents of AuthKey_*.p8 with literal \n, OR path via APNS_AUTH_KEY_PATH (preferred in prod).
APNS_AUTH_KEY=
APNS_AUTH_KEY_PATH=
# Bundle id / APNs topic for this instance's iOS app.
APNS_TOPIC=<com.example.app>
# sandbox | production
APNS_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
APNS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=10

# --- Adapty subscription webhook (ADR-029) -----------------------------------
# POST /v1/billing/adapty/webhook authorizes a static bearer secret
# (Authorization: Bearer <ADAPTY_WEBHOOK_SECRET>, constant-time compare like admin/preview).
#
# ADAPTY_WEBHOOK_SECRET — SECRET, high-entropy (>= 32 bytes), PER-INSTANCE, isolated from every
#   other secret. Empty => the endpoint returns 500 (mis-configured). NEVER commit a real value.
#   It MUST equal the value the operator sets in the Adapty dashboard webhook Authorization header.
#   CLONE NOTE (ADR-017 §Мульти-инстанс): a clone uses its OWN fresh secret — never share between
#   instances; the same fresh value also goes into that instance's Adapty dashboard.
#   Provision (per instance, ON THE SERVER — see §provisioning at bottom of this file):
#     openssl rand -hex 32   ->  /opt/<instance>/.env  ->  restart api  ->  Adapty UI (Bearer).
ADAPTY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<set-per-instance, must match Adapty dashboard; openssl rand -hex 32>
# Adapty product -> credits map (JSON {vendor_product_id: tokens}); NOT a secret, but must match
# the Adapty product configuration. Empty {} => every event uses the fallback grant below.
ADAPTY_PRODUCT_TOKENS={"weekly_xxx":1000,"yearly_yyy":1000}
# Fallback grant (integer > 0) when vendor_product_id is absent from ADAPTY_PRODUCT_TOKENS.
# Separate from SUBSCRIPTION_CREDITS_PER_PERIOD (StoreKit path) for independent calibration.
ADAPTY_SUBSCRIPTION_TOKENS_GRANT=1000

# --- BYOK active model (ADR-016) ---------------------------------------------
BYOK_DEFAULT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# --- Admin auth (ADR-009) — SECRET, isolated, high-entropy -------------------
ADMIN_API_SECRET=<openssl rand -base64 32>
# Previous secret kept valid during rotation (grace period); empty outside rotation.
ADMIN_API_SECRET_PREV=
ADMIN_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=10
ADMIN_SIZE_LIMIT_BODY=8192

# --- Website builder / preview (ADR-010) — SECRET, isolated HMAC key --------
PREVIEW_URL_SECRET=<openssl rand -base64 32>
PREVIEW_URL_TTL_SECONDS=900
PREVIEW_MAX_FILE_BYTES=1048576
PREVIEW_MAX_PROJECT_BYTES=10485760
PREVIEW_MAX_FILES=200
MAX_SERVER_TOOL_ROUNDS=16

# --- Trusted reverse-proxy = the EXTERNAL Traefik (docs/05-security.md anti-spoofing) ----
# must-configure-before-launch: set to the docker network `web` subnet so per-IP rate limiting
# sees the real client IP from Traefik's X-Forwarded-For (not Traefik's own IP). Find the
# subnet ON THE SERVER:
#   docker network inspect web  ->  .[0].IPAM.Config[].Subnet  (typically 172.x.0.0/16)
# Empty => X-Forwarded-For is ignored and only the socket peer (Traefik) is seen — rate limit
# would then be per-Traefik-IP and effectively global (broken). See ADR-017.
TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS=<web-network-subnet-cidr, e.g. 172.18.0.0/16>
TRUSTED_PROXY_HOP_COUNT=1

# --- DB connection pool (per process) ----------------------------------------
# Effective conns ~= (DB_POOL_SIZE + DB_MAX_OVERFLOW) * gunicorn_workers(4) * replicas(1)
# = (10 + 5) * 4 * 1 = 60 < Postgres max_connections (100). Recompute if you scale workers/replicas.
DB_POOL_SIZE=10
DB_MAX_OVERFLOW=5
DB_POOL_TIMEOUT=30
DB_POOL_RECYCLE=1800

# --- API documentation (R7) — hide schema in prod (prod-checklist, Q-007-1 group) --------
DOCS_ENABLED=false

# --- Observability -----------------------------------------------------------
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# SECRET: if set, GET /metrics requires X-Scrape-Token == this value (else 403).
METRICS_SCRAPE_TOKEN=<openssl rand -base64 32>

# =============================================================================
# ADAPTY_WEBHOOK_SECRET provisioning (per instance, ADR-029) — operator runbook.
# Run ON THE SERVER (87.239.135.154, root). Per-instance: repeat for the instances of the LIVE
# INSTANCES roster at the top of this file, each with its OWN fresh secret. That roster is NOT
# restated here on purpose — a second copy would silently skip the next instance added. veltrio is
# DECOMMISSIONED and must NOT be provisioned.
#
#   1. Generate a fresh high-entropy secret for THIS instance:
#        SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
#   2. Write it into the instance .env (replace the placeholder line; never commit .env):
#        cd /opt/<instance>            # THIS instance's /opt/<dir> from the LIVE INSTANCES roster
#        # set ADAPTY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=$SECRET in /opt/<instance>/.env
#   3. Restart api to pick up the new env (migrate not needed for this var):
#        docker compose -p <instance> -f docker-compose.prod.yml --env-file .env up -d --no-build api
#   4. In the Adapty Dashboard for THIS instance's app: configure the webhook URL
#        https://<SERVICE_DOMAIN>/v1/billing/adapty/webhook
#      and set the Authorization header to:  Bearer <the same $SECRET>.
#   5. Verify: a 401 means the bearer values differ; a 500 means the env secret is empty/not loaded.
#
# Do NOT reuse one ADAPTY_WEBHOOK_SECRET across instances — this runbook's secret is per-instance
# and fresh (docs/07-deployment.md §Clone `.env`-контракт, row `ADAPTY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`). The only
# contract-level exception to freshness is the LLM provider service key (rows `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`/
# `OPENAI_API_KEY`); it does not extend to this secret. Do NOT store the real secret in the repo
# or image.
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# Apple root CA provisioning for REAL StoreKit JWS verification — operator runbook.
# Run ON THE SERVER (87.239.135.154, root). Per-instance: `/opt/<instance>` of THIS instance is
# taken from the LIVE INSTANCES roster at the top of this file. That roster is NOT restated here on
# purpose — a second copy would silently skip the next instance added. veltrio is DECOMMISSIONED
# and must NOT be provisioned.
#
# WHO MUST RUN IT — decided by a PREDICATE over an existing source, not by intent. Read it at
# docs/07-deployment.md §Prod-readiness checklist (must-configure-before-launch), the item
# «STOREKIT_TEST_MODE=false + Apple root CA, реальный APPSTORE_BUNDLE_ID, заведённые IAP-продукты»,
# together with that section's applicability note ("применяется к КАЖДОМУ действующему инстансу
# отдельно"; the live set = the registry table docs/07-deployment.md §CI/CD-контракт: INSTANCES-loop,
# a decommissioned instance is excluded there explicitly):
#   * instance IS in that registry table AND accepts (or is about to accept) real users
#     => this runbook is MANDATORY for it — the checklist marks the item «Блокер публичного запуска»;
#   * instance IS in that registry table AND is still MVP/staging (no real users; the same checklist
#     marks that state as STOREKIT_TEST_MODE=true)
#     => it MAY defer this runbook and keep its certs dir EMPTY;
#   * instance is NOT in that registry table (decommissioned / not provisioned)
#     => do NOT provision anything for it at all.
# Fail-closed while deferred: an EMPTY certs dir means _load_roots() == [] , so the real StoreKit
# path cannot mark any transaction verified (422) — deferring never silently accepts a purchase, and
# the empty bind-mount is benign (the container starts normally). Adding an instance therefore needs
# NO edit of this runbook: its obligation follows from the registry table + the checklist above.
#
#   1. Ensure the cert dir exists for THIS instance (it ships in the repo via certs/appstore/.gitkeep,
#      so `git pull` already created it — this is just a safety check):
#        cd /opt/<instance>            # THIS instance's /opt/<dir> from the LIVE INSTANCES roster
#        mkdir -p certs/appstore
#   2. Download Apple's PUBLIC root CA (AppleRootCA-G3, DER .cer) into it:
#        curl -fsSL -o certs/appstore/AppleRootCA-G3.cer \
#             https://www.apple.com/appleca/AppleRootCA-G3.cer
#      (source page: https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/). Optional integrity check:
#        openssl x509 -inform DER -in certs/appstore/AppleRootCA-G3.cer -noout -subject -issuer
#        # expect subject/issuer CN = "Apple Root CA - G3" (self-signed root).
#   3. Make sure STOREKIT_TEST_MODE is NOT true on this instance (.env): real path requires
#        STOREKIT_TEST_MODE=false  (and STOREKIT_TEST_SECRET empty). Prod default is already false.
#   4. Recreate api to mount the now-populated dir (mounts are fixed at container create time —
#      a running container will NOT see a newly-added file without recreate):
#        docker compose -p <instance> -f docker-compose.prod.yml --env-file .env up -d --no-build api
#   5. Verify the root loaded (WITHOUT a real Apple transaction):
#      (a) the api container can read the cert as the non-root user:
#            docker exec <instance>-api-1 ls -l /etc/appstore-certs
#            docker exec <instance>-api-1 sh -c 'head -c 0 /etc/appstore-certs/AppleRootCA-G3.cer && echo READABLE'
#      (b) a self-minted HS256 "transaction" now FAILS with 422 (test-mode is OFF) — same as a
#          forged real transaction. POST a dummy HS256 JWS to the verify endpoint and expect 422
#          ("StoreKit JWS signature invalid"); previously (test-mode on) it would 200. A real
#          ES256/x5c transaction from the app then verifies against the loaded root.
#      (c) the readiness/health probe stays green (GET /ready, GET /health) — loading roots at
#          startup must not crash the app:
#            docker inspect <instance>-api-1 --format '{{.State.Health.Status}}'   # -> healthy
#
# Do NOT commit the .cer to the repo (provisioned on the server). It is PUBLIC, but the source of
# truth is Apple; keep the host dir as the only place it lives. An instance still allowed to defer
# by the predicate above simply leaves its own certs dir EMPTY (test-mode / fail-closed).
# =============================================================================
